== (I-a) n=1, every normalized cocycle (= every section of every class) and every lift of swap (H)
  C=Z2, lifts trivial on C: 8 cocycles, 16 (cocycle, lift) pairs; sign update additive in 0; bit-linear into Z2 in 0
  C=Z4, lifts trivial on C: 64 cocycles, 128 (cocycle, lift) pairs; sign update additive in 0; bit-linear into Z4 in 0
  C=Z4, lifts INVERTING on C: 64 cocycles, 128 (cocycle, lift) pairs; sign update additive in 32; bit-linear into Z4 in 64
  [W] reason: for any lift of S acting trivially on C with Su = v, Sv = u, omega(u,v) = 1:  g(u+v) - g(u) - g(v) = beta(v,u) - beta(u,v) = -(m/2) != 0,
      while an additive g (and a bit-linear g at disjoint-support u, v) gives 0.
